# 5. Use formal logic and simulation to test the architecture

This is where your research approach can deliver substantial value. We should use different verification methods for different classes of problem.

A. Constraint and consistency analysis

Express invariants such as “a committee's geographical reference must belong to the permitted organisation” and “an assignment cannot have an end time before its start time.”

Check whether the constraints contradict one another or leave important cases undefined.

B. State-transition simulation

Simulate Membership admission and ending, committee appointment and removal, geographical moves, role changes, and authorization decisions. Check that forbidden states cannot be reached through valid transitions.

C. Legacy-data reconciliation simulation

Create representative records for every conflicting legacy representation. Compare alternative reconciliation policies and measure how many records become valid, remain ambiguous, or require human adjudication.

D. Concurrency and tenant-isolation simulation

Test simultaneous appointments, membership ending during authorization, changes to geographical hierarchy during a check, duplicate commands, and attempts to cross organisation boundaries.

### Example: an invariant

Suppose the approved rule says an active committee assignment requires current Membership.

Let:

- \\(A(p,c,t)\\) mean person \\(p\\) has an effective assignment to committee \\(c\\) at time \\(t\\).
- \\(M(p,o,t)\\) mean person \\(p\\) has current Membership in organisation \\(o\\) at time \\(t\\).
- \\(O(c)\\) identify the organisation owning committee \\(c\\).

The candidate invariant is:

\\[ A(p,c,t)\Rightarrow M(p,O(c),t) \\]

This is only valid if the business owners approve that rule. Some political or organisational structures may permit external advisers, honorary positions, or other exceptions.

A simulation should test counterexamples and boundary conditions, including whether the rule applies at appointment time only or continuously throughout tenure. That distinction matters: checking eligibility once at appointment does not guarantee eligibility remains valid later.

### What simulation must deliver

- A list of invariants and their approved or provisional status.
- Counterexamples demonstrating contradictory rules or invalid states.
- Evidence that expected valid scenarios remain reachable.
- Results for concurrent operations and organisation boundaries.
- A distinction between model-level evidence and tests of the real Laravel implementation.
- A record of assumptions that still require business decisions.

Simulation does not prove the architecture is correct in every possible situation. It helps us discover defects and demonstrate specific properties within a defined model.

